WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.850
The Preamble opens with:

2
00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:03.450
We, the people of India.

3
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.343
The authority starts with us.

4
00:00:05.843 --> 00:00:07.726
It calls India a sovereign,

5
00:00:07.726 --> 00:00:10.515
socialist, secular, democratic republic.

6
00:00:10.965 --> 00:00:13.150
But socialist and secular

7
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.510
weren't in the text adopted

8
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.258
on 26 November 1949.

9
00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:19.866
The 42nd Amendment added

10
00:00:19.866 --> 00:00:21.170
them in 1976.

11
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.900
Then come four aims:

12
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.865
justice, liberty, equality,

13
00:00:24.865 --> 00:00:25.901
and fraternity.

14
00:00:26.351 --> 00:00:29.338
In Kesavananda Bharati, in 1973,

15
00:00:29.438 --> 00:00:30.833
the Supreme Court treated

16
00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:32.340
the Preamble as part of the

17
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.065
Constitution.

18
00:00:33.515 --> 00:00:36.205
In November 2024, it dismissed

19
00:00:36.205 --> 00:00:38.805
challenges to the 1976 words:

20
00:00:38.925 --> 00:00:40.470
the amending power extends

21
00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:41.421
to the Preamble.

22
00:00:41.871 --> 00:00:43.279
Read it word by word.

23
00:00:43.479 --> 00:00:44.930
Some words have dates.

24
00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:46.326
Your turn.

25
00:00:46.626 --> 00:00:49.165
On which date was the Constitution adopted?
